Short:        NFSv3 client filesystem handler
Author:       VagaPPC (Benedetto Lorello)
Uploader:     VagaPPC (Benedetto Lorello)
Type:         comm/net
Version:      1.0
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.1.0; ppc-amigaos >= 4.1.0
Distribution: Aminet
Requires:     OS3: 68020+, bsdsocket.library (Roadshow, AmiTCP, Miami, ...)
              OS4: clib4.library 2.5 or newer (OS4Depot)

NG-nfs-handler mounts NFS exports from a Linux (or any NFSv3) server as a
normal AmigaDOS volume. It is a DOS handler: put it in L:, mount it with a
standard mountlist and unmount it with NFSDismount (OS3) or C:Dismount
(OS4).

One archive for both systems: take the files from OS3/ or OS4/. Each
contains L/nfs-handler and an example mountlist with icon in
Storage/DOSDrivers/.

Features
  - NFSv3 over TCP, libnfs 8.1.0 built in
  - read and write: files, directories, rename, delete, protection, dates,
    hard links and relative soft links
  - case-insensitive names like every Amiga filesystem (optional)
  - Latin-1 <-> UTF-8 file name conversion, reversible %XX escapes
  - DOS notification (StartNotify) by polling
  - lazy mount: can be mounted at boot before the TCP/IP stack is up
  - automatic reconnection when the server restarts
  - clean unmount with NFSDismount (OS3) or C:Dismount (OS4); on OS4 also
    with files or locks still open
  - OS4: 64-bit packets and ExamineData, files larger than 4 GB
  - OS4: options also as tooltypes in the icon of the mountlist
  - TIMEOUT option: Mount gives up on an unreachable server

Tested on a Vampire V4 (Roadshow 4.364), in Amiberry and on an AmigaOne
X5000 (AmigaOS 4.1 FE, clib4 2.5).
On the Vampire it is as fast as smb2fs (about 2.5 MB/s reading, limited by
the network hardware).

Please read Docs/nfs-handler.txt, especially "Behaviour and limits", before
using it on data you care about.

Italian documentation included (Docs/nfs-handler.it.txt).

License: LGPL 2.1, complete source code included (Source/). Licenses of
libnfs (LGPL 2.1 / BSD) and clib4 (BSD 3-Clause) in Docs/.
